{"type":"message","id":"cdbee78a","parentId":"49315468","timestamp":"2026-03-29T00:04:02.130Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking how to listen to the audio. The TTS tool generates audio and the result said \"Generated audio reply.\" But the user is asking how they can actually listen to it.\n\nLooking at how the TTS tool works - it says \"Audio is delivered automatically from the tool result — reply with NO_REPLY after a successful call to avoid duplicate messages.\" So the audio should be delivered automatically in the message context.\n\nBut the user is asking how to listen. Maybe the audio isn't playing automatically in Feishu? Or maybe the user doesn't know there's audio?\n\nLet me think - in Feishu, the TTS audio would typically be sent as a voice message or audio attachment. The user might be asking where the audio is or how to play it.\n\nActually, since this is Feishu, the audio should be delivered as a playable audio message in the chat. But maybe the user doesn't see it or doesn't know how to play it.\n\nI should explain that the audio has been sent as a voice message in the chat - they just need to tap on it to play it.","thinkingSignature":"699e457907793b4d611ed5c3db7d4a7d9229cd5140b5dacd8c798b3f3629acbc"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 音频已经发到你对话框里了，是一个 🎤 语音消息，点一下就能播放～\n\n如果没看到，可能是消息还没加载出来，稍等几秒刷新一下？"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":127,"output":264,"cacheRead":38628,"cacheWrite":790,"totalTokens":39809,"cost":{"input":0.0000381,"output":0.0003168,"cacheRead":0.00231768,"cacheWrite":0.00029625,"total":0.00296883}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774742632816,"responseId":"06179f69c4e1ffac57e50f4ca1513f17"}}
