{"type":"message","id":"6b1974ea","parentId":"e81b4b6d","timestamp":"2026-03-29T00:15:20.232Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Oh I see - the user wants the AUDIO to be in Chinese, not just the text. The problem is that the TTS tool seems to be generating English audio even when the text is Chinese. \n\nThe issue is with the TTS tool itself - it might not be configured correctly for Chinese. Let me check the TTS configuration or try a different approach.\n\nActually, looking at the TTS tool, it just takes text and converts to speech. The underlying TTS service should handle Chinese text naturally. But it seems like it's detecting the language incorrectly or using an English voice for Chinese text.\n\nLet me check if there's a way to force Chinese language in the TTS tool, or if there's a configuration issue.","thinkingSignature":"21ad4f6c8bd733da3dd479d078219754ea028e0069ca86805e5859df16cdfb6f"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 明白了！抱歉我理解错了 🙏\n\n问题是TTS工具把中文读成英文了——它可能默认用了英文语音。\n\n让我查查有没有配置可以改成中文语音：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_94jfjmopgi36_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -r \"tts\\|voice\\|language\\|zh\" ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json 2>/dev/null | head -30"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":127,"output":240,"cacheRead":44269,"cacheWrite":736,"totalTokens":45372,"cost":{"input":0.0000381,"output":0.000288,"cacheRead":0.00265614,"cacheWrite":0.000276,"total":0.00325824}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774743313616,"responseId":"0617a21251e02c7990ba0277ed9f1157"}}
