{"type":"message","id":"ecba482a","parentId":"b12a4e78","timestamp":"2026-03-29T01:11:51.552Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is frustrated that I keep sending file paths/addresses instead of the actual audio files. They want me to just send the file directly. \n\nLooking at what happened:\n- When I called `message action=send` with `media=/tmp/openclaw/tts-new.mp3`, it actually worked and sent a voice message\n- But before that, when I used the `tts` tool, it returned \"Generated audio reply\" but the audio wasn't sent to them\n\nSo the issue is that the TTS tool doesn't automatically send the audio to the user in Feishu - it just generates it and returns a text message. I have to manually use the message tool to send it.\n\nThe solution is: after using `tts` tool, I should then use `message action=send` with the audio file to deliver it to them. But the TTS tool doesn't return the file path - it just says \"Generated audio reply\".\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the TTS tool result - it said \"Generated audio reply.\" This is the text that appears in the tool result. But the actual audio was generated and... I need to find where it was saved.\n\nLet me check what happens - the TTS tool generates an audio file but doesn't tell me the path. The message was sent as text \"Generated audio reply\" rather than as a voice message.\n\nThe fundamental issue is that the TTS tool is designed for platforms where it can automatically send the audio (like Telegram), but for Feishu, it just generates the file and returns a text indicator.\n\nFor now, I need to:\n1. Use exec to call edge-tts directly to generate the mp3\n2. Then use message send with asVoice=true to send it\n\nThis is the workflow I've been doing manually. The user is asking if I can always do this - and yes I can! I just need to remember to do it every time.\n\nActually wait - the user asked \"以后你能直接发文件吗\" - \"can you send files directly in the future?\" They might be asking if I can make it automatic so I don't send file addresses.\n\n\nI should acknowledge their frustration and clarify that I'll always use the exec + message workflow to deliver audio files directly as voice messages, rather than just sharing file paths.","thinkingSignature":"dcfd2fcc3b860d078fa1d9c219f93e4782e35a9f82b13570c78b07fad51f4611"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 明白了！以后我会这样做：\n\n1. 用 exec 调用 edge-tts 生成中文音频\n2. 用 message 工具的 `asVoice` 参数直接发语音消息给你\n\n不会再发文件地址了！每次都是直接发能播放的语音 🎵\n\n抱歉之前给你添麻烦了 😅"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":143,"output":535,"cacheRead":97764,"cacheWrite":1130,"totalTokens":99572,"cost":{"input":0.0000429,"output":0.000642,"cacheRead":0.00586584,"cacheWrite":0.00042375000000000003,"total":0.006974489999999999}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774746695511,"responseId":"0617af486d133d59890f61c957804831"}}
